\trowd\trgaph108\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx1560\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx3120\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx4680\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx6240\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx7800\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx9360{\pard\intbl\sa0 Ryall (2003). Subjective Rationality, Self\u8211?Confirming Equilibrium, and Corporate Strategy \u183? doi ({\f1 https://doi.org/10.1287/mnsc.49.7.936.16380})\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 overlaps\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 introduction\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 no (0/3 yes)\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 no (0/3 yes)\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 A formal theory of subjective rationality and self-confirming equilibrium in which erroneous counterfactual beliefs are never contradicted by equilibrium play, so that suboptimal strategies and stable performance differences among competing firms persist.\cell}\row
